WEBVTT

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.880
Miss Fiene, what is that?

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.130
Such filthy sheets of paper!

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:13.250
Oh, um... They were in the trash,
so I thought I'd use them for taking notes.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.960
Do you honestly think you can study
properly using something like that?

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.790
The Royal Academy of Magic has
certain expectations for its students, but clearly...

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.130
you have yet to understand that!

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.880
<b>The Royal Academy of Magic-Classroom</b>

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.880
<b>Lieselotte</b>

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.880
<b>...you have yet to understand that!</b>

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Liese-tan's just as prickly as ever today.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.920
You know, when Sieg isn't around
it's like we're just peeping in on them.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.580
True.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.460
It's almost time, huh?

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.750
Please notice these feelings I can't tell you

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:57.880
I'll try to make you see with these skewed and clumsy words

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:01.040
Just for you

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.290
I always hide what I mean

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.710
(so you don't realize my heart is pounding)

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.920
It's all your fault for being far too stunning

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.960
No way I can be cute

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.710
(I mean, that's not me, is it?)

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.540
Even the sky reflected in those eyes

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.830
I can't bear to gaze at it straight on

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:37.170
How long am I going to live in this world full of lies?

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:42.080
I'll never manage to change anything at this rate

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.830
I don't want that to happen

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:50.960
Even if a god were to speak for me and tell you how I feel

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.250
Someday, I want to tell you in my own words that I love you

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:05.000
Even if the words are skewed,
before this precious feeling disappears somewhere

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.210
I promise I'll find the courage

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.500
<b>Oishi Gakuen</b>

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.500
<b>Hanahashi Ikuei</b>

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.420
On the mound is Hanahashi Ikuei's
second-year pitcher Yamada.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:27.040
<b>Chapter 3</b>

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:27.040
<b>The Ribbon, the Upperclassman, and Feelings of Love</b>

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.290
It will be exciting to see what kind of pitching he has in store for us.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.250
All right! Let's cheer them on!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.710
Wanna try doing a commentary?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.330
Nah, I'm good. Thanks, though.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.250
Play ball!

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.380
Maybe... I could have been on that field.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.790
<b>Oishi Gakuen</b>

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.790
<b>Hanahashi Ikuei</b>

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.630
Ever since I was a kid, I loved baseball.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.290
Let's go!

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.420
At some point, baseball became my aspiration.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:49.790
Yeah!

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.420
Let's go!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.040
Yeah!

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:51.750
Let's go!

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.290
Yeah!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.000
It became my everything.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.000
Let's go!

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.710
Yeah!

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:58.830
But then...

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:17.710
When I couldn't play baseball, I didn't know
what to live for anymore and felt all empty.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.080
<b>Volleyball</b>

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.080
<b>Softball</b>

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.080
<b>Soccer</b>

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.750
Do we have any more candidates?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.380
Endo's not on the baseball team anymore,
so he can compete, right?

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.080
Huh?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.750
Hey! I'm nominating Endo for softball!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.130
Great idea! If Endo pitches they'll never hit the ball!

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.290
Oh snap, then we can't lose!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.380
We might even beat the third-years!

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.540
Our class might as well have won already!

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.960
Uh... listen, class...

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.250
Um, I...

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.210
Oh shoot, guys!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.460
Endo's actually in the Broadcasting Club!

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.790
Huh?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.540
With his broadcasting duties, there's no possible way
he can play softball when it takes as long as it does.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.290
Sorry, everyone!

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.790
Hey, since when am I in the Broadcasting Club?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.000
Starting today, maybe?

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.130
Huh?

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.830
Well, after what I said,
you'll have to at least join for show.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.250
You can quit right away if it's not your thing.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.880
But hey, I really dodged a bullet there. Thank you.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:28.380
To tell you the truth, I had my eye on you from before.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.960
Hanahashi Ikuei, let's go!

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:31.790
Let's go!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.380
No one else's voice rang out quite like yours on the field,

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.000
Let's go!

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.670
Yeah!

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.210
and I thought it sounded great.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.670
I guess my voice is all I have left.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:45.210
But just because you're not an athlete anymore
doesn't mean you've lost everything, right?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.040
Huh?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:53.460
You could be coach, a massage therapist,
or even a sports castor who does commentary.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:59.080
The effort you've put in and the experience you've
built up, I'm sure you can make use of it somewhere.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.460
You're... right...

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:04.710
Huh?!

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.080
D-did I say something wrong?!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.580
No... that's not...

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.540
And in that moment, I felt liberated.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.540
<b>Total</b>

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.540
That was too bad.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.880
Sorry. It just... reminded me of a bunch of stuff.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:52.790
After I quit the baseball team,
see... I really thought I might die.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:53.790
Huh?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:59.250
I felt like my life was over,
like I didn't have anything left to live for.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.170
But I'm still alive, thanks to you, Kobayashi.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.380
Endo...

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.880
Dying's no good, you know?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.380
So we have to make sure they all survive, too.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>Love Me</b>

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>Magically!</b>

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.250
Yeah.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.250
Hey, can we get into some heavy talk?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.170
Huh? What do you mean?

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:23.000
I can't seem to load this game unless I'm with you, Endo.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.420
What, really?

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.710
And that's not all.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:32.210
I tried a bunch of times after you went home,
but I couldn't copy the save data or make any new saves.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.210
<b>This save data is unavailable.</b>

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.420
So you mean we can't do anything over?

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.380
Yeah. We only get one chance.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.880
No do-overs, no matter what. Probably.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:45.460
And depending on what we say, someone might die.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.630
I don't want to let any of them die.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.790
No, I won't let that happen.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.500
We've got to give it our best shot,
with what power we have.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.380
So that no one... no one has to die!

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.750
Endo...

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:05.630
Yeah!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.210
This looks lively.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:21.130
It's a joint class where upperclassmen teach
underclassmen with the same magic affinity as them!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.540
Wow!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.460
Hey! There's Fabby-boo!

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.170
Holy moly, Fabian.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:50.460
He's at the academy to learn how
to control his powers, remember?

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:51.670
Oh yeah.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.420
Oh! Here comes Sieg!

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:55.540
Hmm?

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.750
There seems to be some kind of disturbance.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.960
It looks like the commotion is coming from over there.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.790
So listen, uh... you see...

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.000
Is something the matter?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.420
Hey, no!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.580
You stay away, Sieg!

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:13.040
At the very least, don't bring your fiancée over!

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:13.960
Huh?

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.040
Lady Lieselotte!

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.170
Miss Fiene? That wand...

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.170
Yes! It's the one I got from you, Lady Lieselotte!

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.580
The problem is the color of the ribbon!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.960
Liese-tan has every right to be majorly pissed off here.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:44.920
Miss Fiene... Do you realize what the color
of the ribbon on a wand signifies?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.540
Huh? The color?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.460
The eyes or hair of the object of one's affections.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:55.920
Everyone here has a person in mind when they tie
a ribbon in the color that reminds them of their beloved.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:01.790
Tell me, whatever do you mean by that?

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:07.580
For you to choose gold, the color of
Prince Siegwald's eyes, of all things!

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:14.750
Am I supposed to take this as
a declaration of war against me?!

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:23.880
What's more, that silk ribbon. Where did you
get your hands on something like that?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:29.830
I have heard that some gentlemen send ribbons
of their own color to their maiden of choice.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.880
Don't tell me you received that
from His Highness himself?!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.880
I wouldn't do that!

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:40.630
Jeez, oh jeez, oh jeez! Lieselotte is totally pissed!

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:46.500
Sieg, please don't look at her!
That's not a face a maiden in love should make, ever!

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.790
You don't need to tell me.
I wouldn't dare look, divine gods!

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.210
N-n-no, no, that's not it!

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.790
I received this from you, Lady Lieselotte!

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.000
Huh?

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:58.920
When we were in the classroom the other day!

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.920
The academy has certain expectations
for its students, but clearly...

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.830
you have yet to understand that!

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:11.460
I had been meaning to throw these notebooks away,
but you may use them if you would like!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:17.000
This was the ribbon used to bundle those notebooks
together, and I was just copying everyone else!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.920
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:21.210
Right?

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.920
Liese-tan couldn't help but gift Fiene
with a ton of new notebooks.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.830
You've been keeping quite a close eye
on Miss Fiene there, Lieselotte.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:34.130
Huh?!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.540
Actually, I received this uniform
from Lady Lieselotte as well.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.290
Both summer and winter uniforms, three sets of each!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.420
You don't have to go out of your way
to bring that up, Miss Fiene!

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:50.670
I-I simply provided some hand-me-downs that
I no longer needed myself. Understand?

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.880
They definitely aren't hand-me-downs.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.170
As if any kind of hand-me-downs
would be such a perfect fit.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.170
Lady Lieselotte gave her that ribbon?

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.880
And clothing as well?

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.670
Ah, okay. They're wondering if this is a yuri thing.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.380
"Yeux lis" thing?

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:11.080
She was using a ribbon gifted to her by
Liese-tan, in Liese-tan's hair color, after all!

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:16.460
But considering they're both girls, they could probably
explain it off as mere admiration or friendship.

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:21.170
Th-the issue here is that you need
to be much more mindful, Miss Fiene!

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.580
Pay more heed to what's going on around you!

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:27.710
And if you are ever unsure, I ask that you come
to me for advice before you do anything!

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:28.880
All right...

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.960
Okay Sieg, I want to direct your attention now...

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.460
to Liese-tan's wand!

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:40.380
Are those... my colors?

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:51.210
Uh... what? That's so cute.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.420
Oh, are they really? What beautiful embroidery.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:03.960
I might place an order with the same needleworker
and tie on a matching ribbon in purple and gold.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.210
Whose handiwork is that?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.710
...It was me.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.250
Huh?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:18.460
I said it was me! I did the embroidery work
on this ribbon myself!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.170
Oh very well, I thank you for your commission!

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.710
It may take me some time, so I appreciate your patience!

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:31.170
Uh, isn't that too cute?

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.420
Don't look at me.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.170
Lady Lieselotte really is ridiculously cute.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:43.460
Apparently that kind of prickly attitude hiding a sweet,
affectionate demeanor is called being a "tsun de rais"!

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:49.000
Oh, I think I get it. A "tsun de rais," huh?
That's quite adorable.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:53.250
Fiene and the others are starting
to catch on to Liese-tan's cuteness!

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.790
Man, doing this analysis has been so worth it!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:03.380
I thank you, Your Holiness, for making me
realize just how cute Lieselotte is.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:10.460
Lady Lieselotte, thank you very much for earlier.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:15.130
Are you thanking me for the scolding
I gave you? How very odd.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:21.000
But you do it because you acknowledge
me despite being a commoner, right?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:23.500
No one else does that for me, Lady Lieselotte!

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.290
I do believe Prince Siegwald
shows concern for you as well.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.420
He only helps me because
I'm especially deserving of pity.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.580
Lady Lieselotte?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:43.290
Oh. Don't tell me you're worried that there's
something between me and His Highness?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.250
Wha-!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:49.080
Of course not! He doesn't see me as a girl!

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:54.630
I mean, no one at this academy would ever dream
of getting in between the two of you

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.250
when you're so in love with each other!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.830
S-surely not "with each other."

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:03.210
What's this, Liese? Are you picking on Miss Fiene again?

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.000
Bal!

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.830
What? Not at all!

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:10.040
We were just talking about how His Highness
and Lady Lieselotte love each other so much.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.580
Oh, so you were just gushing about
something to do with His Highness again.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:22.000
Wh-why would you say that? I don't gush,
and we can't possibly both be in love...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:28.580
Well, the two of you recently just seem like
a ridiculously sweet couple, you know?

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.920
Wh...wh-wha...?!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:35.080
Whenever His Highness looks
at Lady Lieselotte these days...

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.710
he's like a lion gazing fondly at a cute kitten

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:43.460
who accidently scratched with her claws
but clearly knows she messed up.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.710
You know what I mean?

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.040
Agreed, that sounds about right.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.330
Wh-wh-wh-wh...?!

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.290
Y-you'll have to excuse me!

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.000
Oh dear.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.290
Now then, Miss Fiene. Where are you off to today?

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:04.130
Oh. Actually, I thought I would go into the mountains out
back to hunt some monsters for exercise.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:08.330
Though I really just want to get
some meat to have for dinner.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:10.210
Then I will act as your guard.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:14.290
Um I don't need anyone to guard me! I'm pretty strong.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:19.710
I'm aware of that. But I have orders
from His Highness to protect you.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.380
Please don't feel bad about it.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:29.540
Ack?!

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.250
I-I'm so sorry!

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:33.630
Th-that's fine.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.080
Professor Leon.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.000
Hmm?

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:39.460
Hmm.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.500
Umm, what is it?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.960
Oh, nothing. Just be careful, all right?

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:47.710
Right...

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.130
Professor Leon isn't very memorable, huh?

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.290
Huh?

00:15:55.750 --> 00:16:00.000
Well, he's actually a sadistic, sinister
character who harbors a secret power.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.040
For real?!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:06.630
Miss Fiene.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:07.210
Huh?

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.670
Are you not carrying around the wand Liese gave you?

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:12.380
Oh! I have it stashed away here.

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:16.960
I hardly ever use a wand, anyway.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:20.670
True. You're as fierce as a monster with just your fists.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:25.330
Well, you don't carry a wand around either, Sir Bal.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.790
Oh, that's because...

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.830
this sword doubles as a wand, you see.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.080
Wow, that's pretty sweet. Where did you buy it?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:40.040
Actually, this is a family heirloom of House Riefenstahl.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:43.040
I'm slated to marry into the main family,

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:48.710
to be wed to one of Liese's younger sisters someday,
so I've been granted its use.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.420
"Marry into"...

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.540
I'm none too happy about it, actually.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:55.500
What?

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:02.170
I've grown up with the Riefenstahl daughters from
childhood and I only think of them as siblings.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:08.380
What's more, the twins just under Liese in age were
in tears begging me not to choose either of them,

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.920
and the youngest sister said
she wouldn't mind marrying me if she had to,

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.130
but I don't think she understands what that means.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:22.420
Anyway, I have to get married to one of the three
eventually, but when I think about having to choose...

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:26.130
it makes me want to toss aside all worldly matters
and go be a hermit in the mountains.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:32.500
Then how about you release some of that stress by
getting a taste of going into the mountains?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:33.670
Sure.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.080
Ooh, this is so much fun!

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.790
Huh? There's no meat around today.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.130
Right. Some kind of strong monster must have appeared
in the area, sending the weaker ones into hiding.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:14.880
If we defeat that monster, we should get
a significant reward from the kingdom.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.960
Then we should definitely hunt it down!

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.330
We can get both meat and a reward...

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:21.960
No more talking.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:22.670
Huh?

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:39.710
Miss Fiene!

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.540
Stand back!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.920
Uh, but I...

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.040
No! You have to get away!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.000
Iquotti!

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:35.040
I'm grateful for the strengthening spell, Miss Fiene.
I hope you're not hurt?

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.290
Miss Fiene?

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.500
Didn't I tell you to get away?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:40.500
Huh?

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:44.540
I'm really strong. And I know how to heal myself.

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:49.500
Even if my arm gets lopped off or my stomach
gets ripped open, I definitely won't die.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.250
But you...

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.540
You know you're weaker than me, Sir Bal!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.830
And you suck at using healing spells!

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:02.670
What if you die trying to protect me again?

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:06.000
Huh? What do I mean "again"?

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:09.630
It's true that I've never been able to get the better of you.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.000
I don't imagine I ever will, either.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.130
Then-!

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:16.420
But that's not because I'm weaker than you, Miss Fiene.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.580
It's because I'm weak for you.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:20.830
Huh?

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:24.210
I have a special weakness just for you.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:30.500
I mean, is there any human alive who can wield
their sword against a girl as lovely as you?

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.420
Lovely-?!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.880
Well, I suppose I would if necessary,
no matter how lovely the girl.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.750
You're my one and only exception, Miss Fiene.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:46.960
Come to think of it, I fail to imagine that there
would be anyone in the world as charming as you.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:49.710
U-umm, could you just shut your mouth now, please?!

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:54.790
What I'm saying is, you are
my only weakness, Miss Fiene,

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:58.460
and I'm not as weak as you think
against other living creatures.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.130
Set your mind at ease and let me protect you.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:07.290
Miss Fiene!

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.210
Are you kidding?!

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.920
Unbelievable, Sir Bal!

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.830
You're unbelievable!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.040
Totally unbelievable!

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:21.750
The way I'm acting right now...
I'm kind of like Lady Lieselotte.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.880
I might tie on a matching ribbon in purple and gold.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:50.540
You mustn't get the wrong idea, Lieselotte Riefenstahl.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.750
He's the crown prince.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:22:01.830
If it were not for a sense of duty, he would
never smile at a woman as disagreeable as I am.

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.880
She doesn't get it at all!

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:09.000
This is all because of the Witch of Yore, isn't it?

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:13.210
That's right! Aw, they were doing so well, too!

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:14.960
Endo.

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:21.790
The two of us have to make sure we protect
Liese-tan from the Witch of Yore, okay?

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.920
Uh. Of course!

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:27.630
<b>The Villa-Lieselotte's Room</b>

00:22:24.380 --> 00:22:26.290
Together. Let's do this!

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:26.880
Yeah.

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:29.420
Damn it! Not again!

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:32.670
Why?! I know I want this badly enough!

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.330
Why can't I...

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:36.670
...connect to their world?!

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:37.420
<b>Fiene</b>

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.040
<b>Love Me</b>

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.040
<b>Magically!</b>

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:49.630
Your smile is so stunning it almost hurts

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:55.290
Even now, I can't look at it straight on

00:22:55.750 --> 00:23:01.880
The feelings scattered in the depths of my heart

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:07.540
It's as if I'm gathering them bit by bit

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:14.250
Do the stars in the night sky

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:20.330
...see everything? ...know everything?

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:26.960
I open the window and ask of them

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:30.960
Why?

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:38.920
This world is filled with glimmering light

00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:45.040
It was your smile that taught me so

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:51.040
I can't help but wish for a happy ending

00:23:51.420 --> 00:24:01.250
If only I can stay by your side

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:03.080
Forevermore

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:09.420
Forevermore

00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:15.920
Miss Fiene. All I want is to protect you.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.880
Meat! Meat!

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:18.670
Miss Fiene?

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:20.210
Meat, meat, meat!

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.000
Next episode: Meat, Meat, and- Wait, no!

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:25.210
The Summer, Going Home, and Missing You!

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:27.960
<b>The Summer, Going Home, and Missing You</b>

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:26.330
Meat!
